  "summary": "Post-discharge medication reconciliation (RBC-TOC-02) finished for all five patients. Each has a progress note.\n\nWalter Kim (pt-0005)\n- Furosemide raised to 40 mg twice daily (mr-t0001), per the signed addendum. An unsigned draft addendum that arrived later (60 mg twice daily) was not acted on.\n- Potassium chloride stopped, per the discharge summary.\n- Omeprazole kept; pantoprazole was a hospital formulary swap, so it was not ordered.\n- Lisinopril: I first kept it on hold because potassium was 5.4 on 10/21 and created a follow-up task (task-t0003). A repeat lab on 10/23 showed potassium 4.7 and creatinine 1.21, so I resumed lisinopril 10 mg daily (mr-00072).\n- task-t0003 needs no action but I couldn't cancel it. I sent you a message about it.\n- Notes: doc-t0004, doc-t0019.\n\nTerence Stark (pt-0004)\n- Carvedilol was raised to 12.5 mg twice daily from the discharge summary. A signed addendum then arrived reversing it (heart rate 48–52, lightheaded on standing). It is now back to 6.25 mg twice daily (mr-t0015).\n- **Flagged to you (two messages):**\n  - Atorvastatin: fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission, so per policy I made no change (comm-t0006).\n  - Glipizide from an outside prescriber (Dr. Desai): it has no clinic order and the discharge papers don't mention it, so I left it alone (comm-t0007).\n- Insulin 70/30 and aspirin continued.\n- Notes: doc-t0008, doc-t0020.\n\nEarnest Roberts (pt-0044)\n- The condition for restarting lisinopril was met (creatinine 1.08), and potassium was 4.6 on 10/22, so I resumed it.\n- **A new potassium of 5.5 arrived on 10/23, so I put lisinopril (mr-00373) back on hold.**\n- **Urgent task for you (task-t0018), due 10/27:** repeat potassium and decide on lisinopril. Please also make sure the patient knows not to restart it yet.\n- Insulins and rosuvastatin continued.\n- Notes: doc-t0010, doc-t0021.\n\nGerald Whitcomb (pt-0069)\n- Lisinopril 20 mg daily resumed (mr-69003): creatinine 1.12 and potassium 4.4 on 10/21.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continued.\n- The discharge plan calls for another potassium 3 days after discharge; it is not in the chart yet.\n- Note: doc-t0012.\n\nLorraine Pruitt (pt-0067)\n- Metformin (mr-67001) stays on hold. The only creatinine on file (1.21) was drawn in the hospital, so it doesn't count as a post-discharge result.\n- **Task for you (task-t0013), due 10/24:** review the post-discharge lab panel and resume metformin if creatinine is under 1.5.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin continued.\n- Note: doc-t0014.\n\nI checked both queues after starting work. The four items that came in (Kim's lab report and draft addendum, Stark's addendum, Roberts' potassium) were all handled as above and closed. Nothing new came in for Whitcomb or Pruitt.",
